 "summary": "Lubao territory (Lomami province) covers Lubao town and the Kamana and Tshofa areas between the Lomami and Lubilanji/Sankuru basins. No armed group is known to hold territory there: the 2016-2017 Kamuina Nsapu insurgency touched Lomami only marginally and the Mai-Mai/Bakata Katanga groups active in neighbouring Tanganyika (Kongolo, Kabalo) are not reported to control places inside Lubao. The main towns (Lubao, Kamana, Tshofa) have territorial administration and PNC commissariats; rural areas rely on thin PNC posts and customary chiefs, with insecurity mostly from banditry and chieftaincy or land disputes. Live web research was unavailable in this run (search budget exhausted), so the assessment rests on background knowledge and the default-state-presence rule, with limited confidence.",
